p.src:
Each upper index contributes one forward Jacobian: $(T')^{mn}
 =\frac{\partial y^m}{\partial x^p}
  \frac{\partial y^n}{\partial x^q}
  T^{pq}.$ The product construction motivates the rule, but the transformation law is the definition of a tensor. A rank-three contravariant tensor would acquire three such Jacobian factors.

