p.src:
The same transformation machinery now applies to the metric. Since the interval is a scalar, it must have the same value in either coordinate system: $\begin{aligned}
 ds^2
 &=g_{mn}(x)\,dx^m dx^n,\\
 dx^m
 &=\frac{\partial x^m}{\partial y^p}\,dy^p.\end{aligned}$ Substitution completes the line that the board leaves unfinished: $g'_{pq}(y)
 =\frac{\partial x^m}{\partial y^p}
  \frac{\partial x^n}{\partial y^q}
  g_{mn}(x(y)).$ Thus $g_{mn}$ is a rank-two covariant tensor.

